{
  "case_id": "2002-02-196",
  "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case concerns the applicability of the Contract Disputes Act to contracts between National Park Service and the private concessioners who contract to provide visitor services and to operate and maintain facilities in more than 100 of our national parks."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Geller, I have a couple of preliminary questions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here we have a regulation that categorically states no NPS -- no National Park Service concession contracts are subject to the CDA. If there -- there are, in fact, some such contracts that are subject to the CDA, as we believe there are, then that regulation is arbitrary and capricious. The agency should have to go back and draft a more refined regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Three. There are, I think, three."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We are harmed, Justice Ginsburg, because it is important for the concessioners to know, at the time that they're deciding whether to bid on a contract and -- and the time they're deciding how much to bid on a contract, what their rights are under that contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, what -- what if the Government contract had a term that simply said, you know, there would be damages for delay, double damages depending on the amount of delay? And you say, well, I -- we don't think the Government is authorized to put that in a contract. Could you challenge that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: Yes. I believe so, Mr. Chief Justice. There is a very large body of Government contracting law -- it's not in the briefs because it wasn't raised -- allowing --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But where is the law? in the cases of this Court? I mean, is it"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: Well, obviously, these -- these cases are generally litigated in the -- in the Court of Federal Claims and in the district courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Geller, you say -- you say it's settled, and please correct me if I'm wrong if -- if Abbott Laboratories has been overtaken. But my notion was that in order to have a pre-enforcement challenge, you had to have a pretty strong claim that you are hurting now, as they were, if they didn't -- if they spent all that money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: Yes. Abbott Laboratories is -- is obviously an APA case. I think we could meet that standard because we need to know now whether we should bid on these contracts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: Well, we brought both an APA cause of action and a challenge under the -- under the Tucker Act, and you know, we would maintain that we can challenge this regulation, and in addition, we can challenge this bid solicitation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Was there any finding in the district court that the inclusion of this provision was critical as to whether or not you'd go ahead with the contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: There was no such --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: -- if you go through one form of remedy or the other in the event of a breach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geller",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GELLER: But it's not binary, Justice Kennedy. Maybe you would still enter into the contract negotiations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What they say then is the Government -- as far as I understand it, the basic point is that this is not a procurement contract regardless of who's entitled to what deference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0021",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: You don't want to pay pre-judgment interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0022",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is this -- is this claim ripe? And why didn't you ever talk about it below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0001-0024",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What about this -- what about the -- the reply? I came in thinking ripeness was a problem, and your brother on the other side gave to me what was a very convincing answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I'm not asking you what the law is exactly. I'm asking you what's the Government's position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we filed a brief in opposition and I think, you know, if -- if we can win on ripeness grounds, that's great too."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's not a big-ticket item. The only three cases in which the -- the CDA has been applied to national park concessions are the three IBCA cases mentioned, and in two of those, the Government wound up winning on the merits, so there was no pre-judgment interest paid. So it's only in that R&R Enterprises case that the Government would have paid any pre-judgment interest in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Elwood",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, just as a statistical matter, 78 percent of concessions contracts do not involve any capital improvements."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ELWOOD",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even though the Government has bare title in these buildings, in a very real sense it doesn't buy them. Every concessioner who builds a building in the national parks under a concessions agreement will have a leasehold surrender interest equal to the construction cost of the building plus inflation minus depreciation. And they cannot be put out of that building by anyone until they are paid that leasehold surrender interest; that is, until the building essentially is bought. As long as a concessioner is operating out of that building, a concessioner will hold the leasehold surrender interest, not the Government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Congress",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Finally, I think it's noteworthy that Congress obviously knew that concessioners would be building buildings under the 1998 act, which was enacted against the backdrop of this regulation setting forth the Park Service's consistently held view that concessions contracts are not procurement contracts. And far from displacing that view, they actually seem to embrace it both in the text of the act and in the legislative history that Justice Breyer mentioned."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Maybe the Park Service wrote that portion of the committee report."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government makes much of the fact that no, quote, Government funds were used here. And I cannot stress enough that that is a phrase that they've invented for the purposes of this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government is the sole beneficiary of the contractual provisions in virtually every concessions contract requiring the construction, repair, and maintenance of facilities in the national parks."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court wishes supplemental briefs on the issue of ripeness, simultaneous briefs, due 3:00 p.m. Friday."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
